        "answer": {
          "short": "Missing entries by row: $-1, -26$; $-12, -10, -8$. Magic sum: $-30$.",
          "worked": "The complete bottom row gives the magic sum:\n$$\\begin{align*}-17+6+(-19)&=-30\\end{align*}$$\nCentre entry, using the diagonal from top-right to bottom-left:\n$$\\begin{align*}-30-(-3)-(-17)&=-30+3+17\\\\&=-10\\end{align*}$$\nTop-left entry, using the other diagonal:\n$$\\begin{align*}-30-(-10)-(-19)&=-30+10+19\\\\&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nTop-middle entry:\n$$\\begin{align*}-30-(-10)-6&=-30+10-6\\\\&=-26\\end{align*}$$\nMiddle-left entry:\n$$\\begin{align*}-30-(-1)-(-17)&=-30+1+17\\\\&=-12\\end{align*}$$\nMiddle-right entry:\n$$\\begin{align*}-30-(-3)-(-19)&=-30+3+19\\\\&=-8\\end{align*}$$\nEvery row, column and diagonal sums to $-30$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
